Experimental thermal conductivities and the derived properties such as thermal diffusivities are reported for ionic liquid 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium thiocyanate (short name is [EMIM][SCN]) in the temperature range from (296 to 365) K at pressures up to 30 MPa. Weak linear temperature decreases of the thermal conductivity was experimentally observed. The effect of pressure on the measured thermal conductivity was studied. The measured thermal conductivity data together with our previous reported density and heat capacity data were used to calculated key derived transport property of [EMIM][SCN] such as thermal diffusivity (
) based on the well-known thermodynamic relation
. Experimental thermal conductivities at atmospheric pressure are in good agreement (deviation within 0.6 % to 4.5 %) with the recent reported data.
